rem Fractions involving the Number of
rem Different Ways a Number can be
rem Expressed as a Sum of Powers of 2
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=175
rem Find the shortened binary expansion
rem of the least n with b(n) / b(n-1)
rem equal to Num / Den, with b(n) the
rem number of sums of powers of 2 that
rem use each power at most twice

use numbers
use sequences
use text
use io
use cli

arg Num integer = 123456789
arg Den integer = 987654321

rem Undo the bit steps of problem 169
rem on (x, y) = (b(n), b(n-1)): a 0 bit
rem came from (x - y, y), a 1 bit from
rem (x, y - x). Subtract in runs, as in
rem the continued fraction, and keep the
rem lengths of the runs of equal bits.
G = Num gcd Den
X = Num // G
Y = Den // G
Runs = array shape 0 fill 0
Q = 0
for X + Y greater 1
  if X greater Y
    Q = (X - 1) // Y
    X -= Q * Y
  else
    Q = Y // X
    Y -= Q * X
  end
  Runs = concat Runs (array Q)
end
Answer = Runs reverse join ","
Answer print
